              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to shake out, then the Telugu for to hang up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కాచు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కాచు — kācu — \"to boil milk; to heat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అమ్మ పొద్దున్నే పాలు కాచింది. amma poddunnē pālu kācindi. Mum boiled the milk early in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): కాచాను, kācānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "For milk and water; అన్నం వండు for rice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కాచు (kācu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 1458 lists Telugu kācu, \"to heat, to warm, to boil\", with Tamil kāy, \"to grow hot\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
