              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మాడ్చు — māḍcu — \"to scorch; to burn food\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఫోనులో మాట్లాడుతూ నేను కూర మాడ్చాను. phōnulō māṭlāḍutū nēnu kūra māḍcānu. Talking on the phone, I burnt the curry."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): మాడ్చాను, māḍcānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మాడు, to get burnt, is its intransitive partner."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మాడ్చు (māḍcu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4801 lists Telugu māḍu, \"to be burnt, to be scorched black\", and māḍ(u)cu, \"to burn, to scorch\"."
            }
